# core.autocrlf=true on a Windows dev machine rewrites checked-out files to
# CRLF. Anything that runs inside the Linux container must stay LF, or the
# kernel reads the shebang as "/bin/sh\r" and the build fails with
# "bad interpreter". Pin those explicitly.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
